LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. Live alarm and runbook both say 6/3; the HCL description now says 3 of 6. The new drift test failed on voter_errors alone before the edit and passes after. make verify locally: only the 17 known pandoc failures under tests/unit/reconciler; Linux CI green. Review advisories left open on purpose: (1) the claim pattern allows at most 2 words between the number and 'periods' or 'window', a floor on the number of claims found guards against it going blind; (2) the mismatch comparison is exercised by the real tree but has no seeded call that drives it directly. The live CloudWatch text changes only when Terraform is applied; that is the linked P4 task.","timestamp":1792841650180009001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1792758374176967484,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6a713bc7-3a72-426b-a0cf-d06db11fab5a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ab07-c603-a94a-419e"},{"link_uuid":"ac8ea219-8d79-4cd2-bad2-cf9d6d8ce55f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"efb8-7e51-4beb-4d57"},{"link_uuid":"43b6e803-db19-45f9-bcfc-b34d1e3f3a05","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"a9d1-c7f3-cfd9-44ff"}],"description":"## Observed problem\n`infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` configures `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.voter_errors` with `evaluation_periods = 6`, `datapoints_to_alarm = 3`, and `period = 300`. Its `alarm_description` still says it pages on \"3 of 5 five-minute periods.\" That text is sent to CloudWatch/SNS and contradicts the deployed threshold.\n\n## Verification (2026-10-24)\n- Live alarm `rebar-gerrit-voter-errors` (us-east-1): EvaluationPeriods 6, DatapointsToAlarm 3, Period 300, TreatMissingData notBreaching; its live description says \"3 of 5 five-minute\" (874 characters).\n- The tuning runbook (`infra/runbooks/alarm-window-tuning.md`) already records this alarm as `300/6/3`, so the description is the stale side.\n- Survey of all 43 alarm blocks: only 2 descriptions contain an \"N of M\" claim, and only `voter_errors` disagrees with its HCL (`review_interrupts_signal_unavailable` says 2 of 4 and is 2 of 4).\n- Longest effective description (after the `<<-` heredoc strips indentation) is 1,021 characters against CloudWatch's 1,024 limit; the edited voter description keeps its length.\n\n## Approach\n1. In `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf`, change \"3 of 5 five-minute periods\" to \"3 of 6 five-minute periods\" in the description. Leave the \"~15 minutes\" claim: 3 consecutive 5-minute breaching buckets of a stuck voter are still 15 minutes.\n2. In `tests/unit/test_alarm_window_tuning.py`, parse each alarm's description and fail when an \"N of M\" (or \"N-of-M\") window claim differs from `datapoints_to_alarm` of `evaluation_periods`. Seed the check with a mismatched example that must be flagged and a matching one that must pass, and keep a floor on the number of claims found so the parser cannot go blind. The 1,024 limit is already enforced by `tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py` (in bytes, the provider's unit), so no second length check is added.\n3. Change no thresholds, dimensions, actions or missing-data behaviour.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` and `tests/unit/test_alarm_window_tuning.py`. Out of scope: applying Terraform to the live alarm (an operator step) and the other alarms' wording.\n\n## Testing\n```\npytest tests/unit/test_alarm_window_tuning.py -q\npytest tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py -q\nterraform fmt -check infra/terraform\nmake verify\n```\nFailure case: before the HCL edit the new drift test fails naming `voter_errors`; the seeded mismatched description must be flagged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The `voter_errors` description in the HCL says 3 of 6 five-minute periods and matches `datapoints_to_alarm` and `evaluation_periods` (checked: new test passes after the edit and fails before it).\n- [x] The drift test covers every alarm and rejects a seeded mismatched description (checked: seeded test).\n- [x] The edited description still fits the provider limit (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py -q` passes).\n- [x] `make verify` is green on the Linux CI gate (`Verified +1` on the Gerrit change).\n\n## Follow-up\nThe live CloudWatch description changes only when an operator applies Terraform; that apply is tracked in its own ticket rather than held open here.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf","reason":"Correct the voter_errors alarm description to 3 of 6 periods"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_alarm_window_tuning.py","reason":"Detect description versus threshold drift and over-long descriptions"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","efb8-7e51-4beb-4d57"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2e5f3685-2868-4c28-b8f5-72fd581175d2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"714b-0b2c-a8f9-468e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Voter error alarm description says 3 of 5 while HCL uses 3 of 6","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0fbe36ad-f604-4a33-aec2-6f8f74911bbc","4ac7ffda-4fef-45b1-b7f0-bcf3bdb2037f","530bbd43-462a-4e01-a7b5-21a5f36be805","ecd30878-a06d-4b40-b1e2-87b8864a2c79","531611c0-5600-4cce-aaf0-724e95fcd0fd","9601d2e7-cf6e-4670-9f8d-2b0f65fb5871","ac8ea219-8d79-4cd2-bad2-cf9d6d8ce55f","13f0ea5d-5c3a-43c8-bb59-8c55987e1898","341e96f9-32d4-4118-b27c-15bdc98f6b10","2e5f3685-2868-4c28-b8f5-72fd581175d2","956ed1b0-145b-4753-adb0-3ac83ff5ef2d","43b6e803-db19-45f9-bcfc-b34d1e3f3a05"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792844327423747089,"uuid":"2a0807d4-25d5-4915-8bf7-fd0f28b460c0"}